You are smarter than the briefing agent. Treat what follows as **non-negotiable product constraints and success outcomes**. Prefer a better implementation, architecture, or UX when it still hits these outcomes. Do not invent affiliate IDs, prices, deals, or secrets. Do not clone third-party deal copy.

## Product
- Live site: https://www.actuallydeals.com — slogan **Deals that are actually good!**
- Queue-first desk at `/admin`. Founder (Michael Margulis / Mike) publishes unless he explicitly asked you to publish.
- Best-deals-first, original writeups, his affiliate links only. Dead deals gray out. Never write “we’re first” on the site.
- House social: X `@actuallydeals`, Instagram `@actuallydeals_` (underscore), Facebook `ActuallyDeals`. Auto-post kill switch; official APIs only; no session scraping.

## Architecture (prefer existing seams)
- Persist only through `src/lib/store.ts`.
- Product photos: plain `<img>` + `src/lib/images.ts` (no `next/image`).
- Parse / ingest: `src/lib/ingest-roundup.ts`, `src/lib/parse-deal.ts` — merchant-tolerant; Amazon bot walls must degrade (ASIN from OP + CDN), not hard-fail.
- Affiliates: `src/lib/affiliate.ts` — strip tracking; empty env ID = clean retailer URL.
- Amazon Store ID / tag: **`actuallydea07-20` only** (never `actuallydeals-20`).
- Rakuten SID **`4745711` is dead** — hard-block; never wrap Newegg with it; no second Rakuten account.
- Ship: GitHub `ActuallyDeals/actually-deals` `main` → Vercel **actually-deals** (hyphen) → www. Leftover no-hyphen Vercel project never gets the domain.
- One packed increment per PR. `npx tsc --noEmit` green; run `npx tsx scripts/verify-parser.mts` when parse/affiliate/copy changes.

## Editorial / price integrity (standing)
- Original voice only. Reject Deal Score / Frontpage / slickdeals / doctorofcredit / hip2save / freebie guy chrome (`looksClonedWriteup`).
- **Always include every source instruction** (qty, which coupon/link to click/activate, SnS, order). Missing a step = customer won’t get the same price.
- Plain titles — no `SnS`, `AC`, `~$`, `[Code] $0* |` jargon.
- Separate numbered stack steps; never invent was-prices.
- DoC: live promo code only.

## Security
- Empty `ADMIN_PASSWORD` hard-fails `/admin`. No default password in repo. No Staff footer. `/admin` noindex.
- Secrets in Vercel env only — never `NEXT_PUBLIC_` passwords, never SSN/EIN/bank in chat or logs.
- Keep baseline security headers; don’t add a CSP that breaks Amazon CDN without verifying.

